⍝ lib/ring.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude, part 16: rings: ℤ/n, ideals, quotient rings, generic ring algorithms, multivariate polynomials and Gröbner bases
⍝ Everything is computed here, on base-(i−1) digit strings; helpers end in _rg.  Residues modulo n are naturals in [0, n).  Ideals of ℤ and of
⍝ ℚ[x] are principal and are given by a generator; the ideals of ℤ/n are lists of their elements.  A multivariate polynomial is a list of terms
⍝ (c, e): c ∈ ℚ[i] the coefficient, e the list of the exponents; the monomial order is a natural number: 0 lexicographic, 1 graded
⍝ lexicographic, 2 graded reverse lexicographic.  Canonical form: terms in decreasing order, like monomials merged, no zero coefficient,
⍝ all exponent lists of one length (the number of variables); the zero polynomial is the empty list.
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 1. the ring ℤ/n
addmod ∶ ℤ → ℤ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ (a + b) mod n, in [0, n)  (n ≥ 1)
addmod ξ η ζ ≔ (mod (⊞ ξ η) ζ)
submod ∶ ℤ → ℤ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ (a − b) mod n, in [0, n)
submod ξ η ζ ≔ (mod (⊟ ξ η) ζ)
mulmod ∶ ℤ → ℤ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ (a · b) mod n, in [0, n)
mulmod ξ η ζ ≔ (mod (⊠ ξ η) ζ)
negmod ∶ ℤ → ℕ → ℕ      ⍝ (−a) mod n, in [0, n)
negmod ξ ζ ≔ (mod (⊖ ξ) ζ)
zunits ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the units of ℤ/n: the a in [0, n) with gcd(a, n) = 1, ascending (ℤ/1 is the zero ring: its unit is 0)
zunits ξ ≔ (filter (κ ↦ (≐ (gcd κ ξ) 1)) (⍳ ξ))
zzerodivisors ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the zero divisors of ℤ/n: the a in [1, n) with gcd(a, n) > 1, ascending
zzerodivisors ξ ≔ (filter (κ ↦ (¬ (≐ (gcd κ ξ) 1))) (upto 1 (⊟ ξ 1)))
znilpotents ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the nilpotent elements of ℤ/n: the multiples of rad(n) in [0, n), ascending (the nilradical)
znilpotents ξ ≔ (filter (κ ↦ (≐ (mod κ (radical ξ)) 0)) (⍳ ξ))
zidempotents ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the idempotents of ℤ/n: the a in [0, n) with a² ≡ a, ascending (2ᵏ of them for k distinct primes)
zidempotents ξ ≔ (filter (κ ↦ (≐ (mod (⊠ κ κ) ξ) κ)) (⍳ ξ))
zideal ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the ideal of ℤ/n generated by a list of integers: its elements, ascending (the multiples of d = gcd(n, generators))
zideal ξ η ≔ ((δ ↦ (⫶ (κ ↦ (⊠ κ δ)) (⍳ (div ξ δ)))) (gcd ξ (gcdlist η)))
zideals ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ all ideals of ℤ/n, one per divisor d of n (the ideal (d)), by increasing d
zideals ξ ≔ (⫶ (δ ↦ (zideal ξ (∷ δ ⊥))) (divisors ξ))
zmaxideals ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the maximal ideals of ℤ/n (= the prime ideals): (p) for every prime p dividing n, by increasing p
zmaxideals ξ ≔ (⫶ (δ ↦ (zideal ξ (∷ δ ⊥))) (primefactors ξ))
zprimeideals ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 ℕ)      ⍝ the prime ideals of ℤ/n: the same as the maximal ideals, as ℤ/n is finite
zprimeideals ξ ≔ (zmaxideals ξ)
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 2. principal ideals of ℤ and of ℚ[x]: the ideal is given by a generator (a polynomial: the monic generator)
idealsum ∶ ℤ → ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ (a) + (b) = (gcd(a, b)), the ideals of ℤ given by generators
idealsum ξ η ≔ (gcd ξ η)
idealintersect ∶ ℤ → ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ (a) ∩ (b) = (lcm(a, b))
idealintersect ξ η ≔ (lcm ξ η)
idealproduct ∶ ℤ → ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ (a)(b) = (|ab|)
idealproduct ξ η ≔ (abs (⊠ ξ η))
idealcontains ∶ ℤ → ℤ → 𝔹      ⍝ (a) ⊇ (b), that is a | b  (0 divides only 0)
idealcontains ξ η ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) (≐ η 0) (≐ (mod η ξ) 0))
idealradical ∶ ℤ → ℕ      ⍝ the radical of the ideal (n) of ℤ: (rad n)
idealradical ξ ≔ (radical ξ)
polyidealsum ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ (f) + (g) in ℚ[i][x]: the monic gcd (a zero generator is ignored)
polyidealsum ξ η ≔ (polygcd ξ η)
polyidealintersect ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ (f) ∩ (g): the monic lcm
polyidealintersect ξ η ≔ (polylcm ξ η)
polyidealproduct ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ (f)(g): the monic product
polyidealproduct ξ η ≔ (polymonic (polymul ξ η))
polyidealcontains ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → 𝔹      ⍝ (f) ⊇ (g), that is f divides g  (the zero polynomial divides only itself)
polyidealcontains ξ η ≔ ((∅ (poly ξ)) (∅ (poly η)) (∅ (polyrem η ξ)))
polyidealradical ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ the radical of the ideal (f): the square-free part, monic
polyidealradical ξ ≔ (sqfree ξ)
polyidealgen ∶ 𝔏 ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ the monic generator of the ideal of ℚ[i][x] generated by the polynomials of the list ([] for the zero ideal)
polyidealgen ξ ≔ (foldl polygcd ⊥ ξ)
polyidealmember ∶ ℚ[i][x] → 𝔏 ℚ[i][x] → 𝔹      ⍝ does p lie in the ideal generated by the polynomials of the list?
polyidealmember ξ η ≔ (polyidealcontains (polyidealgen η) ξ)
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 3. the quotient ring ℚ[i][x]/(f): its elements are the polynomials of degree < deg f
qrreduce ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ qrreduce(f, a) = a mod f, the representative of a in ℚ[i][x]/(f)
qrreduce ξ η ≔ (polyrem η ξ)
qradd ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ qradd(f, a, b) = a + b in ℚ[i][x]/(f)
qradd ξ η ζ ≔ (polyrem (polyadd η ζ) ξ)
qrsub ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ a − b in ℚ[i][x]/(f)
qrsub ξ η ζ ≔ (polyrem (polysub η ζ) ξ)
qrneg ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ −a in ℚ[i][x]/(f)
qrneg ξ η ≔ (polyrem (polyneg η) ξ)
qrmul ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ a · b in ℚ[i][x]/(f)
qrmul ξ η ζ ≔ (polyrem (polymul η ζ) ξ)
⍝ the inverse of a modulo f from the extended Euclid algorithm s·a + t·f = gcd; [] when gcd(a, f) ≠ 1
qrinv ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ the inverse of a in ℚ[i][x]/(f), [] when a is not a unit (gcd(a, f) is not constant) or a = 0
qrinv ξ η ≔ ((σ ↦ ((∧ (∅ (⌄ (◀ σ))) (¬ (∅ (◀ σ)))) (polyrem (◀ (▶ σ)) ξ) ⊥)) (polyegcd (polyrem η ξ) ξ))
qrisunit ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → 𝔹      ⍝ is a a unit of ℚ[i][x]/(f)?  (gcd(a, f) = 1)
qrisunit ξ η ≔ (¬ (∅ (qrinv ξ η)))
qrpow ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x] → ℤ → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ aⁿ in ℚ[i][x]/(f) by squaring (n < 0: the power of the inverse; [] if a is not a unit)
qrpow ξ η ζ ≔ ((≺ ζ 0) (polypowmod (qrinv ξ η) (⊖ ζ) ξ) (polypowmod η ζ ξ))
qrdimension ∶ ℚ[i][x] → ℕ      ⍝ the dimension of ℚ[i][x]/(f) over ℚ[i]: deg f
qrdimension ξ ≔ (max 0 (deg ξ))
qrisfield ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔹      ⍝ is ℚ[x]/(f) a field?  (f irreducible over ℚ)
qrisfield ξ ≔ (isirreducible ξ)
⍝ Chinese remainder theorem in ℚ[i][x]: the polynomial of degree < Σ deg mₖ congruent to rₖ modulo mₖ (pairwise coprime moduli); [] if not coprime
polycrt ∶ 𝔏 ℚ[i][x] → 𝔏 ℚ[i][x] → ℚ[i][x]      ⍝ polycrt(rs, ms): p ≡ rₖ (mod mₖ) for all k, of degree < Σ deg mₖ ([] if the moduli are not pairwise coprime)
polycrt ξ η ≔ ((Μ ↦ ((τs ↦ ((∀ₗ (u ↦ (¬ (∅ u))) (⫶ (θ ↦ (◀ θ)) τs)) (polyrem (foldl polyadd ⊥ (⫴ (r θ ↦ (polymul (polymul r (◀ θ)) (▶ θ))) ξ τs)) Μ) ⊥)) (⫶ (m ↦ ((Μₖ ↦ (⊗ (qrinv m Μₖ) Μₖ)) (◀ (polydivmod Μ m)))) η))) (foldl polymul (∷ 1 ⊥) η))
⍝ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ 4. multivariate polynomials
ℚ[i][𝐱] ∶ 𝒦      ⍝ polynomials in several variables over ℚ[i]: a list of terms (c, e), c the coefficient and e the list of exponents
(≣ ℚ[i][𝐱] (𝔏 (𝔓 ℚ[i] (𝔏 ℕ))))
⍝ lexicographic comparison of exponent lists of equal length, and the three monomial orders as three-way comparisons
lex_rg ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔒
lex_rg ξ η ≔ (ξ (a as ↦ (η (b bs ↦ ((⋚ a b) ⋖ (lex_rg as bs) ⋗)) ≖)) ≖)
mcmp_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔒
mcmp_rg ο ξ η ≔ ((≐ ο 0) (lex_rg ξ η) ((⋚ (sumof ξ) (sumof η)) ⋖ ((≐ ο 1) (lex_rg ξ η) (lex_rg (reverse η) (reverse ξ))) ⋗))
eqe_rg ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔹
eqe_rg ξ η ≔ (eqlist ≐ ξ η)
eqterm_rg ∶ α → α → 𝔹
eqterm_rg ξ η ≔ (∧ (≐ (◀ ξ) (◀ η)) (eqe_rg (▶ ξ) (▶ η)))
⍝ insertion into a list of terms sorted in decreasing order (keeping equal monomials); like terms merged; arities
ins_rg ∶ ℕ → α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
ins_rg ο θ ξ ≔ (ξ (h t ↦ ((mcmp_rg ο (▶ θ) (▶ h)) (∷ h (ins_rg ο θ t)) (∷ θ ξ) (∷ θ ξ))) (∷ θ ⊥))
mrg_rg ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
mrg_rg ξ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (ι (θ′ ι′ ↦ ((eqe_rg (▶ θ) (▶ θ′)) (mrg_rg (∷ (⊗ (⊜ (⊞ (◀ θ) (◀ θ′))) (▶ θ)) ι′)) (∷ θ (mrg_rg ι)))) (∷ θ ⊥))) ⊥)
pad_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
pad_rg ν ξ ≔ (⧺ ξ (replicate (⊟ ν (ℓ ξ)) 0))
ar_rg ∶ 𝔏 α → ℕ
ar_rg ξ ≔ (foldl (σ θ ↦ (max σ (ℓ (▶ θ)))) 0 ξ)
arl_rg ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → ℕ
arl_rg ξ ≔ (foldl (σ θ ↦ (max σ (ar_rg θ))) 0 ξ)
⍝ the canonical form with a given number of variables ν; of one polynomial, of two, of a list
nn_rg ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
nn_rg ο ν ξ ≔ (filter (θ ↦ (¬ (≐ (◀ θ) 0))) (mrg_rg (foldr (θ ι ↦ (ins_rg ο (⊗ (⊜ (◀ θ)) (pad_rg ν (▶ θ))) ι)) ⊥ ξ)))
nrm_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
nrm_rg ο ξ ≔ (nn_rg ο (ar_rg ξ) ξ)
nl_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 (𝔏 α)
nl_rg ο ξ ≔ ((ν ↦ (⫶ (nn_rg ο ν) ξ)) (arl_rg ξ))
n2_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔓 (𝔏 α) (𝔏 α)
n2_rg ο ξ η ≔ ((ν ↦ (⊗ (nn_rg ο ν ξ) (nn_rg ο ν η))) (max (ar_rg ξ) (ar_rg η)))
mpoly ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ mpoly(o, p): the canonical form of a list of terms in the monomial order o (0 lex, 1 grlex, 2 grevlex): sorted decreasingly, like terms merged, zero terms dropped, exponent lists padded
mpoly ξ η ≔ (nrm_rg ξ η)
⍝ arithmetic on canonical polynomials of one arity
one_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α
one_rg ξ ≔ (∷ (⊗ 1 (replicate ξ 0)) ⊥)
mtm_rg ∶ α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
mtm_rg θ ξ ≔ (⫶ (κ ↦ (⊗ (⊜ (⊠ (◀ θ) (◀ κ))) (⫴ ⊞ (▶ θ) (▶ κ)))) ξ)
sca_rg ∶ ℚ[i] → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
sca_rg ξ η ≔ ((≐ ξ 0) ⊥ (⫶ (θ ↦ (⊗ (⊜ (⊠ ξ (◀ θ))) (▶ θ))) η))
add_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
add_rg ο ξ η ≔ (ξ (t ts ↦ (η (u us ↦ ((mcmp_rg ο (▶ t) (▶ u)) (∷ u (add_rg ο ξ us)) ((κ ↦ ((≐ κ 0) (add_rg ο ts us) (∷ (⊗ κ (▶ t)) (add_rg ο ts us)))) (⊜ (⊞ (◀ t) (◀ u)))) (∷ t (add_rg ο ts η)))) ξ)) η)
sub_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
sub_rg ο ξ η ≔ (add_rg ο ξ (sca_rg 11101 η))
mul_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
mul_rg ο ξ η ≔ (foldr (θ ι ↦ (add_rg ο (mtm_rg θ η) ι)) ⊥ ξ)
pow_rg ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 α → ℕ → 𝔏 α
pow_rg ο ν ξ η ≔ ((≐ η 0) (one_rg ν) (mul_rg ο ξ (pow_rg ο ν ξ (⊟ η 1))))
mpadd ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ p + q in the monomial order o
mpadd ξ η ζ ≔ ((π ↦ (add_rg ξ (◀ π) (▶ π))) (n2_rg ξ η ζ))
mpsub ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ p − q
mpsub ξ η ζ ≔ ((π ↦ (sub_rg ξ (◀ π) (▶ π))) (n2_rg ξ η ζ))
mpneg ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ −p
mpneg ξ η ≔ (sca_rg 11101 (nrm_rg ξ η))
mpscale ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i] → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ c·p
mpscale ξ η ζ ≔ (sca_rg η (nrm_rg ξ ζ))
mpmul ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ p · q
mpmul ξ η ζ ≔ ((π ↦ (mul_rg ξ (◀ π) (▶ π))) (n2_rg ξ η ζ))
mppow ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ pⁿ (p⁰ = 1)
mppow ξ η ζ ≔ ((φ ↦ (pow_rg ξ (ar_rg φ) φ ζ)) (nrm_rg ξ η))
mpeval ∶ ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔏 ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]      ⍝ the value of p at a point (a list of values for the variables)
mpeval ξ η ≔ (foldl (σ θ ↦ (⊞ σ (⊠ (◀ θ) (foldl (π pe ↦ (⊠ π (^ (◀ pe) (▶ pe)))) 1 (⫴ ⊗ η (▶ θ)))))) 0 ξ)
mpdegree ∶ ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℤ      ⍝ the total degree of p (−1 for the zero polynomial)
mpdegree ξ ≔ (foldl (σ θ ↦ (max σ (sumof (▶ θ)))) 11101 (nrm_rg 0 ξ))
mpderiv ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ the partial derivative of p with respect to variable j (0-based)
mpderiv ξ η ζ ≔ (⫶ (θ ↦ (⊗ (⊜ (⊠ (◀ θ) (nth (▶ θ) ζ))) (⫴ (κ x ↦ ((≐ κ ζ) (⊟ x 1) x)) (⍳ (ℓ (▶ θ))) (▶ θ)))) (filter (θ ↦ (¬ (≐ (nth (▶ θ) ζ) 0))) (nrm_rg ξ η)))
mpsubst ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ mpsubst(o, p, j, q): p with the variable j replaced by the polynomial q
mpsubst ξ η ζ υ ≔ ((π ↦ ((ν ↦ (foldl (σ θ ↦ (add_rg ξ σ (mul_rg ξ (∷ (⊗ (◀ θ) (⫴ (κ x ↦ ((≐ κ ζ) 0 x)) (⍳ ν) (▶ θ))) ⊥) (pow_rg ξ ν (▶ π) (nth (▶ θ) ζ))))) ⊥ (◀ π))) (ar_rg (◀ π)))) (n2_rg ξ η υ))
mplc ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i]      ⍝ the leading coefficient of p in the order o (0 for the zero polynomial)
mplc ξ η ≔ ((φ ↦ ((∅ φ) 0 (◀ (hd φ)))) (nrm_rg ξ η))
mplm ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔏 ℕ      ⍝ the exponent list of the leading monomial of p in the order o ([] for the zero polynomial)
mplm ξ η ≔ ((φ ↦ ((∅ φ) ⊥ (▶ (hd φ)))) (nrm_rg ξ η))
⍝ division with remainder by a list of polynomials (the multivariate division algorithm).  φ: the divisors (canonical, one arity); the
⍝ state is the current dividend ξ, the quotients κ (parallel to φ) and the remainder ρ collected so far
mdv_rg ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔹
mdv_rg ξ η ≔ (∀ₗ (κ ↦ κ) (⫴ ⩽ ξ η))
fst_rg ∶ 𝔏 𝔹 → 𝔏 𝔹
fst_rg ξ ≔ (ξ (b bs ↦ (b (∷ ⊤ (⫶ (x ↦ ⊥) bs)) (∷ ⊥ (fst_rg bs)))) ⊥)
dvd_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 α → 𝔓 (𝔏 (𝔏 α)) (𝔏 α)
dvd_rg ο φ ξ κ ρ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ ((ζ ↦ ((∃ₗ (b ↦ b) ζ) ((f ↦ ((q ↦ (dvd_rg ο φ (sub_rg ο ξ (mtm_rg q f)) (⫴ (b Q ↦ (b (add_rg ο Q (∷ q ⊥)) Q)) (fst_rg ζ) κ) ρ)) (⊗ (⊜ (÷ (◀ θ) (◀ (hd f)))) (⫴ ⊟ (▶ θ) (▶ (hd f)))))) (hd (concat (⫴ (b f ↦ (b (∷ f ⊥) ⊥)) (fst_rg ζ) φ)))) (dvd_rg ο φ ι κ (⧺ ρ (∷ θ ⊥))))) (⫶ (f ↦ ((∅ f) ⊥ (mdv_rg (▶ (hd f)) (▶ θ)))) φ))) (⊗ κ ρ))
nf_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
nf_rg ο φ ξ ≔ (▶ (dvd_rg ο φ ξ (⫶ (f ↦ ⊥) φ) ⊥))
mpdivide ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔓 (𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱]) ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ mpdivide(o, p, F): (quotients, remainder) with p = Σ qₖ·fₖ + r, no term of r divisible by a leading monomial of F, lm(qₖ fₖ) ≤ lm(p) (the division algorithm: the divisors in the order given; a zero divisor never divides)
mpdivide ξ η ζ ≔ ((ν ↦ (dvd_rg ξ (⫶ (nn_rg ξ ν) ζ) (nn_rg ξ ν η) (⫶ (f ↦ ⊥) ζ) ⊥)) (max (ar_rg η) (arl_rg ζ)))
mpreduce ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ the remainder of p on division by the list F
mpreduce ξ η ζ ≔ (▶ (mpdivide ξ η ζ))
⍝ S-polynomial, Buchberger's algorithm (product criterion; pairs in the order they arise), minimal and reduced bases
spoly_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
spoly_rg ο f g ≔ ((m ↦ (sub_rg ο (mtm_rg (⊗ (÷ 1 (◀ (hd f))) (⫴ ⊟ m (▶ (hd f)))) f) (mtm_rg (⊗ (÷ 1 (◀ (hd g))) (⫴ ⊟ m (▶ (hd g)))) g))) (⫴ max (▶ (hd f)) (▶ (hd g))))
spoly ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱] → ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ the S-polynomial of two polynomials: (m/lt f)·f − (m/lt g)·g, m the lcm of the leading monomials ([] if either is zero)
spoly ξ η ζ ≔ ((π ↦ ((∨ (∅ (◀ π)) (∅ (▶ π))) ⊥ (spoly_rg ξ (◀ π) (▶ π)))) (n2_rg ξ η ζ))
cop_rg ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔹
cop_rg ξ η ≔ (∀ₗ (κ ↦ κ) (⫴ (a b ↦ (∨ (≐ a 0) (≐ b 0))) ξ η))
mon_rg ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
mon_rg ξ ≔ (sca_rg (÷ 1 (◀ (hd ξ))) ξ)
buch_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 (𝔓 ℕ ℕ) → 𝔏 (𝔏 α)
buch_rg ο γ π ≔ (π (pr rest ↦ ((f g ↦ ((cop_rg (▶ (hd f)) (▶ (hd g))) (buch_rg ο γ rest) ((s ↦ ((∅ s) (buch_rg ο γ rest) ((n ↦ (buch_rg ο (⧺ γ (∷ (mon_rg s) ⊥)) (⧺ rest (⫶ (k ↦ (⊗ k n)) (⍳ n))))) (ℓ γ)))) (nf_rg ο γ (spoly_rg ο f g))))) (nth γ (◀ pr)) (nth γ (▶ pr)))) γ)
pairs_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔓 ℕ ℕ)
pairs_rg ξ ≔ (concat (⫶ (j ↦ (⫶ (a ↦ (⊗ a j)) (⍳ j))) (⍳ ξ)))
gb_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 (𝔏 α)
gb_rg ο ξ ≔ ((γ ↦ (buch_rg ο γ (pairs_rg (ℓ γ)))) (⫶ mon_rg (filter (f ↦ (¬ (∅ f))) (nl_rg ο ξ))))
groebner ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ a Gröbner basis of the ideal generated by the polynomials, in the monomial order o (Buchberger's algorithm, product criterion; monic elements, in the order found; not minimal in general — use reducedgroebner for the canonical basis)
groebner ξ η ≔ (gb_rg ξ η)
⍝ minimal: drop g when another element's leading monomial divides lm(g) (of equal leading monomials the first one stays); reduced: every element
⍝ reduced by the others; sorted by increasing leading monomial
minim_rg ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 (𝔏 α)
minim_rg γ ≔ (concat (⫴ (k g ↦ ((∃ₗ (b ↦ b) (⫴ (j h ↦ (∧ (¬ (≐ j k)) (∧ (mdv_rg (▶ (hd h)) (▶ (hd g))) (∨ (¬ (eqe_rg (▶ (hd h)) (▶ (hd g)))) (⩽ j k))))) (⍳ (ℓ γ)) γ)) ⊥ (∷ g ⊥))) (⍳ (ℓ γ)) γ))
insl_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 (𝔏 α)
insl_rg ο g ξ ≔ (ξ (h t ↦ ((mcmp_rg ο (▶ (hd g)) (▶ (hd h))) (∷ g ξ) (∷ g ξ) (∷ h (insl_rg ο g t)))) (∷ g ⊥))
sorted_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 (𝔏 α)
sorted_rg ο ξ ≔ (foldr (g acc ↦ (insl_rg ο g acc)) ⊥ ξ)
red_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 (𝔏 α)
red_rg ο γ ≔ ((μ ↦ (sorted_rg ο (⫴ (k g ↦ (mon_rg (nf_rg ο (concat (⫴ (j h ↦ ((≐ j k) ⊥ (∷ h ⊥))) (⍳ (ℓ μ)) μ)) g))) (⍳ (ℓ μ)) μ))) (minim_rg γ))
reducedgroebner ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ the reduced Gröbner basis of the ideal in the monomial order o: monic, minimal, every term of every element reduced by the others, sorted by increasing leading monomial — unique for the ideal and the order ([] for the zero ideal, [1] for the unit ideal)
reducedgroebner ξ η ≔ (red_rg ξ (gb_rg ξ η))
idealmember ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔹      ⍝ does p lie in the ideal generated by the polynomials (its remainder on a Gröbner basis is zero)?
idealmember ξ η ζ ≔ ((ν ↦ (∅ (nf_rg ξ (gb_rg ξ (⫶ (nn_rg ξ ν) ζ)) (nn_rg ξ ν η)))) (max (ar_rg η) (arl_rg ζ)))
idealequal ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔹      ⍝ do two lists of polynomials generate the same ideal? (equal reduced Gröbner bases)
idealequal ξ η ζ ≔ ((ν ↦ (eqlist (eqlist eqterm_rg) (reducedgroebner ξ (⫶ (nn_rg ξ ν) η)) (reducedgroebner ξ (⫶ (nn_rg ξ ν) ζ)))) (max (arl_rg η) (arl_rg ζ)))
isgroebner ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔹      ⍝ is the list a Gröbner basis of the ideal it generates? (every S-polynomial reduces to zero)
isgroebner ξ η ≔ ((γ ↦ (∀ₗ (pr ↦ (∅ (nf_rg ξ γ (spoly_rg ξ (nth γ (◀ pr)) (nth γ (▶ pr)))))) (pairs_rg (ℓ γ)))) (filter (f ↦ (¬ (∅ f))) (nl_rg ξ η)))
eliminate ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝔏 ℚ[i][𝐱]      ⍝ eliminate(k, F): a basis of the polynomials of the ideal generated by F that do not involve the first k variables (the elements free of x₀ … xₖ₋₁ of the reduced lexicographic Gröbner basis)
eliminate ξ η ≔ (filter (f ↦ (∀ₗ (θ ↦ (∀ₗ (e ↦ (≐ e 0)) (take ξ (▶ θ)))) f)) (reducedgroebner 0 η))
⍝ text: "3*x^2*y - z + 1/2" with the variables x, y, z, w, u, v (then x6, x7 …)
vn_rg ∶ ℕ → 𝕊
vn_rg ξ ≔ ((≺ ξ 111011100) (nth (∷ "x" (∷ "y" (∷ "z" (∷ "w" (∷ "u" (∷ "v" ⊥)))))) ξ) (∷ 'x' (dec ξ)))
pw_rg ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝕊
pw_rg ξ η ≔ ((≐ η 1) (vn_rg ξ) (⧺ (vn_rg ξ) (∷ '^' (dec η))))
mono_rg ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝕊
mono_rg ξ ≔ (foldr (s acc ↦ ((∅ acc) s (⧺ s (∷ '*' acc)))) ⊥ (concat (⫴ (j k ↦ ((≐ k 0) ⊥ (∷ (pw_rg j k) ⊥))) (⍳ (ℓ ξ)) ξ)))
tm_rg ∶ α → 𝔹 → 𝕊
tm_rg θ ρ ≔ ((μ ↦ ((rl_pl (◀ θ)) ((τ c ↦ (⧺ (ρ (τ "-" ⊥) (τ " - " " + ")) ((∅ μ) (showq c) ((≐ c 1) μ (⧺ (showq c) (∷ '*' μ)))))) (≺ (◀ θ) 0) (abs (◀ θ))) (⧺ (ρ ⊥ " + ") (∷ '(' (⧺ (showc (◀ θ)) (∷ ')' ((∅ μ) ⊥ (∷ '*' μ)))))))) (mono_rg (▶ θ)))
ps_rg ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔹 → 𝕊
ps_rg ξ ρ ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (⧺ (tm_rg θ ρ) (ps_rg ι ⊥))) ⊥)
mpstr ∶ ℕ → ℚ[i][𝐱] → 𝕊      ⍝ the polynomial in human notation in the order o, leading term first: "x^2*y - 3*z + 1/2", "0"
mpstr ξ η ≔ ((φ ↦ ((∅ φ) "0" (ps_rg φ ⊤))) (nrm_rg ξ η))
